{
  "bookId": "PSA",
  "chapter": 77,
  "bookEnglish": "Psalms",
  "bookChineseSimplified": "诗篇",
  "bookChineseTraditional": "詩篇",
  "verses": [
    {
      "verse": "1",
      "en": {
        "text": "My cry goes to God! I cry to God for help, and for him to listen to me.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "我要向 神发声呼求；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "我要向上帝發聲呼求；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "2",
      "en": {
        "text": "In the day of my trouble I sought the Lord. My hand was stretched out in the night, and didn’t get tired. My soul refused to be comforted.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "我在患难之日寻求主；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "我在患難之日尋求主；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "3",
      "en": {
        "text": "I remember God, and I groan. I complain, and my spirit is overwhelmed.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "我想念 神，就烦燥不安；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "我想念上帝，就煩燥不安；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "4",
      "en": {
        "text": "You hold my eyelids open. I am so troubled that I can’t speak.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "你叫我不能闭眼；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "你叫我不能閉眼；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "5",
      "en": {
        "text": "I have considered the days of old, the years of ancient times.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "我追想古时之日，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "我追想古時之日，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "6",
      "en": {
        "text": "I remember my song in the night. I consider in my own heart; my spirit diligently inquires:",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "我想起我夜间的歌曲，扪心自问；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "我想起我夜間的歌曲，捫心自問；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "7",
      "en": {
        "text": "“Will the Lord reject us forever? Will he be favorable no more?",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "难道主要永远丢弃，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "難道主要永遠丟棄，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "8",
      "en": {
        "text": "Has his loving kindness vanished forever? Does his promise fail for generations?",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "难道他的慈爱永远穷尽，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "難道他的慈愛永遠窮盡，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "9",
      "en": {
        "text": "Has God forgotten to be gracious? Has he, in anger, withheld his compassion?”",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "难道 神忘记开恩，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "難道上帝忘記開恩，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "10",
      "en": {
        "text": "Then I thought, “I will appeal to this: the years of the right hand of the Most High.”",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "我便说：这是我的懦弱， 至高者右手之年代。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "我便說：這是我的懦弱， 至高者右手之年代。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "11",
      "en": {
        "text": "I will remember the LORD’s deeds; for I will remember your wonders of old.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "我要提说耶和华所行的；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "我要提說耶和華所行的；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "12",
      "en": {
        "text": "I will also meditate on all your work, and consider your doings.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "我也要思想你的经营，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "我也要思想你的經營，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "13",
      "en": {
        "text": "Your way, God, is in the sanctuary. What god is great like God?",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "神啊，你的作为是洁净的；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "上帝啊，你的作為是潔淨的；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "14",
      "en": {
        "text": "You are the God who does wonders. You have made your strength known among the peoples.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "你是行奇事的 神；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "你是行奇事的上帝；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "15",
      "en": {
        "text": "You have redeemed your people with your arm, the sons of Jacob and Joseph.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "你曾用你的膀臂赎了你的民， 和的子孙。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "你曾用你的膀臂贖了你的民， 和的子孫。",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "16",
      "en": {
        "text": "The waters saw you, God. The waters saw you, and they writhed. The depths also convulsed.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "神啊，诸水见你，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "上帝啊，諸水見你，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "17",
      "en": {
        "text": "The clouds poured out water. The skies resounded with thunder. Your arrows also flashed around.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "云中倒出水来；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "雲中倒出水來；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "18",
      "en": {
        "text": "The voice of your thunder was in the whirlwind. The lightnings lit up the world. The earth trembled and shook.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "你的雷声在旋风中；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "你的雷聲在旋風中；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "19",
      "en": {
        "text": "Your way was through the sea, through the great waters. were not known.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "你的道在海中；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "你的道在海中；",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "20",
      "en": {
        "text": "You led your people like a flock, by the hand of Moses and Aaron.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "你曾借和的手引导你的百姓，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "你曾藉和的手引導你的百姓，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    }
  ]
}